From e19a8e0f6151303ba74eb4e7adb0e8402e64f025 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Azathothas <ajamx101@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:43:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] GitHub #713, #740: pod doctor and the start of netns run
 one probe

canrun.rs has the one rule of the netns backend: the test hook, a TCP
connect to 127.0.0.1 that is not refused (T-382), and unshare of a
network namespace (with or without a user namespace) with lo and a TUN
or a veth pair. auto, --backend netns, --backend netns-kernel and
pod doctor use it.

- #713: pod doctor has the row "TCP connect (127.0.0.1)". Its verdict
  of netns (and of netns-kernel) is the rule above, with the cause in
  the text line. Where auto takes seccomp because netns cannot run, the
  line of --name-backend does not say "use --backend netns".
- #740: --backend netns (and netns-kernel) run the probe before the
  start. A refused namespace gives one line with the cause and the next
  step ("use --backend seccomp, or run the pod where an unprivileged
  user namespace works"), exit 3, and a report with backend null, hold
  none and that line as the reason.

Tests: tests/pod_backend_line.rs
the_doctor_and_the_start_agree_where_netns_cannot_run (unshare refused
by a seccomp filter; TCP connect refused by Landlock), and
canrun::tests::the_netns_rule_and_its_line.
